Subject: Display persisted bundle selections in Hyva CSP order details
Upstream: hyva-themes/magento2-default-theme-csp 1.5.3
Commit: e0c6bd9a008996b9dc8f7c58b447cec921760fdf
Original-SHA256: 5cf925b05a3b5e04c5c45d004aa129b5e5ae7fd0e44d97b7c6b1b0d011bce012

The order pager supplies parent rows. The default renderer omits bundle_options,
so customer order details lose selected components. Render the stored selections
with HTML escaping; retain pagination and all original order assertions.
This patch is applied only to the isolated validation shop, not by the installer.

--- a/vendor/hyva-themes/magento2-default-theme-csp/Magento_Sales/templates/order/items/renderer/default.phtml
+++ b/vendor/hyva-themes/magento2-default-theme-csp/Magento_Sales/templates/order/items/renderer/default.phtml
@@ -43,6 +43,19 @@
                     </div>
                 <?php endforeach; ?>
             <?php endif; ?>
+            <?php foreach (($block->getOrderItem()->getProductOptions()['bundle_options'] ?? []) as $option): ?>
+                <div class="text-sm flex mt-1">
+                    <span><?= $escaper->escapeHtml($option['label']) ?>:</span>
+                    <span class="ml-1">
+                        <?php foreach ($option['value'] as $selection): ?>
+                            <span class="block">
+                                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml($localeFormatter->formatNumber((float) $selection['qty'])) ?>
+                                &times; <?= $escaper->escapeHtml($selection['title']) ?>
+                            </span>
+                        <?php endforeach; ?>
+                    </span>
+                </div>
+            <?php endforeach; ?>
             <?php /* downloadable */ ?>
             <?php if ($links = $block->getLinks()): ?>
                 <div class="item options my-2">
